1
00:01:00,144 --> 00:01:04,190
TAEKANG GROUP TASK FORCE
MANAGING DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

2
00:01:26,879 --> 00:01:27,713
Yoon Yi-jun.

3
00:02:21,684 --> 00:02:25,312
FIVE HOURS AGO

4
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:41,161
Republic of Korea Air Force One
will be landing shortly.

5
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:43,581
All relevant personnel,

6
00:02:43,664 --> 00:02:45,749
please wait in your designated seats.

7
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:53,382
The president and the economic delegation
will conclude

8
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:55,718
their Middle East tour
with their return home today.

9
00:02:55,801 --> 00:02:58,804
For the first time, the heads
of the five largest business groups

10
00:02:58,888 --> 00:03:01,015
-accompanied the president.
-It's Yoon Yi-jun.

11
00:03:01,098 --> 00:03:02,141
-Yoon Yi-jun.
-Mr. Yoon.

12
00:03:02,224 --> 00:03:06,353
Managing Director Yoon Yi-jun's
successful handling of foreign affairs

13
00:03:06,437 --> 00:03:09,607
drove up Taekang's stock price.

14
00:03:10,274 --> 00:03:13,277
In particular, with Taekang's chairman,
Yoon Tae-sik, being ill,

15
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,780
Managing Director Yoon Yi-jun
has drawn attention

16
00:03:16,864 --> 00:03:19,450
as the youngest member of the delegation

17
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:21,368
and the potential successor of Taekang.

18
00:03:21,452 --> 00:03:24,997
During this trip which emphasized economic
partnerships, Mr. Yoon was praised

19
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,624
for driving economic soft power

20
00:03:26,707 --> 00:03:30,336
and elevating not only the corporation's,
but also the nation's global status.

21
00:03:31,962 --> 00:03:34,632
Great work, Mr. President.

22
00:03:34,715 --> 00:03:35,674
Thank you.

23
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:01,825
I've prepared your usual tea.
It's been steeped for 3 minutes at 90°C.

24
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:15,756
It's been steeped
for 3 minutes and 10 seconds at 88°C.

25
00:04:17,508 --> 00:04:18,509
I won't drink it.

26
00:04:19,301 --> 00:04:20,302
The photos.

27
00:04:22,638 --> 00:04:24,473
The overseas trip was a success.

28
00:04:24,556 --> 00:04:25,599
Next.

29
00:04:25,683 --> 00:04:27,309
You supported the president well.

30
00:04:27,393 --> 00:04:28,602
Stop.

31
00:04:28,686 --> 00:04:29,603
Zoom in.

32
00:04:30,896 --> 00:04:33,273
Your jawline looks especially sharp today.

33
00:04:33,357 --> 00:04:34,942
You're the star tonight.

34
00:04:35,025 --> 00:04:36,694
Is that the right answer?

35
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:37,987
Well…

36
00:04:43,575 --> 00:04:46,120
Promotion for the 7 Series,
which is coming out next month.

37
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:47,746
It can be seen clearly, sir.

38
00:04:47,830 --> 00:04:50,207
Make sure every news outlet
runs this photo.

39
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:51,458
Yes, sir.

40
00:04:51,542 --> 00:04:53,502
You had a thorough plan from the start.

41
00:04:53,585 --> 00:04:56,088
I'll report back to you within 30 minutes.

42
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:58,966
Attorney Kim Si-hyun
is going to pick you up himself.

43
00:05:10,769 --> 00:05:11,895
SEOUL AIR BASE

44
00:05:11,979 --> 00:05:13,689
Listen up here.

45
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:15,983
As if landing a 3-trillion-won deal
wasn't enough,

46
00:05:16,066 --> 00:05:18,986
you used the president
as a backdrop for a free ad?

47
00:05:20,362 --> 00:05:23,490
There was a red carpet,
the cameras were rolling,

48
00:05:24,408 --> 00:05:25,701
and we had the perfect model.

49
00:05:26,994 --> 00:05:28,037
Why waste it?

50
00:05:29,705 --> 00:05:31,415
I should really work harder.

51
00:05:31,498 --> 00:05:33,876
If the successor of Taekang Group
is working this hard,

52
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:35,335
I should be working harder.

53
00:05:35,919 --> 00:05:36,879
Is something wrong?

54
00:05:37,796 --> 00:05:41,842
No. Just doing a final review
of the photos sent by Secretary An.

55
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:42,801
It's Secretary Jung.

56
00:05:44,178 --> 00:05:46,430
His last name is neither An nor Kim.
It's Jung.

57
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:48,724
His name is Jung Da-woon.

58
00:05:48,807 --> 00:05:51,685
He's been on the TF team
working with you for the past five years.

59
00:05:51,769 --> 00:05:54,313
Thanks for such useful information.

60
00:05:56,857 --> 00:05:59,401
Take me to the office.
I'll submit the final report myself.

61
00:05:59,485 --> 00:06:02,279
And tell me
why you came to pick me up yourself.

62
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:04,031
You must be tired, honey.

63
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:06,408
I want to make sure
you're well taken care of.

64
00:06:50,369 --> 00:06:51,411
Are you okay?

65
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,833
Thank you.

66
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:57,876
Excuse me.

67
00:06:57,960 --> 00:07:01,255
-He's so cool.
-Can I add you to my social media, sir?

68
00:07:01,922 --> 00:07:03,048
I don't do social media.

69
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,760
-You have a promise ring.
-I'm a police officer.

70
00:07:06,844 --> 00:07:08,303
I'll hold the money for you.

71
00:07:08,387 --> 00:07:09,930
Are you really a police officer?

72
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:11,807
I'm telling you I am.

73
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:13,225
-Here.
-A police officer?

74
00:07:13,308 --> 00:07:15,185
-I'm from Dongbu Police.
-That little…

75
00:07:15,269 --> 00:07:16,478
Take a look.

76
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:19,439
I'll hold the money
until the investigation is--

77
00:07:19,523 --> 00:07:21,900
Hey. Lieutenant Park Dong-hwan?

78
00:07:21,984 --> 00:07:24,153
-Damn it!
-You!

79
00:07:24,236 --> 00:07:27,156
-Let go of me!
-Ma'am, are you okay?

80
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:29,616
My money.

81
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:31,326
-My money.
-Wan-gu.

82
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:32,619
Come to the intersection.

83
00:07:32,703 --> 00:07:33,829
Hey…

84
00:07:37,249 --> 00:07:38,417
Again?

85
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:39,334
Hey!

86
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:41,503
Get back here!

87
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:43,630
Hey!

88
00:07:44,298 --> 00:07:45,757
Stop following me!

89
00:07:45,841 --> 00:07:47,176
Stop right there!

90
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:51,263
Hey, you punk!

91
00:07:52,556 --> 00:07:54,933
Sir, we're in trouble.

92
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:57,936
-A cop is…
-And you brought him here, you bastard?

93
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,062
Let's go!

94
00:07:59,146 --> 00:08:00,397
Get in, quickly!

95
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:12,826
Who does he think he is?

96
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:16,705
I had a heart attack thinking
it was a real cop.

97
00:08:17,206 --> 00:08:19,166
Why are you scared of some kid?

98
00:08:21,001 --> 00:08:22,753
Hand over the old lady's money.

99
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,546
An imprisonment of at least one year,

100
00:08:24,630 --> 00:08:26,548
or a fine at least triple the proceeds.

101
00:08:27,132 --> 00:08:29,092
That's the sentence for voice phishing.

102
00:08:29,593 --> 00:08:32,721
Did you get all that
from watching videos all day?

103
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:34,806
Hey, kid. Just go open the door.

104
00:08:35,933 --> 00:08:37,184
-Let's go!
-Yes, sir.

105
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:38,518
Damn it.

106
00:08:41,230 --> 00:08:43,982
Sir, are you okay?

107
00:08:44,066 --> 00:08:45,275
Let go of me!

108
00:08:45,359 --> 00:08:48,195
Hey. Do you have a death wish?

109
00:08:49,154 --> 00:08:50,447
You little…

110
00:08:53,909 --> 00:08:55,452
You started it.

111
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:58,163
From now on, it's self-defense.

112
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:01,541
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

113
00:09:02,209 --> 00:09:03,794
What the hell?

114
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:05,254
Sir!

115
00:09:05,337 --> 00:09:07,214
Hurry up and take your weapons out!

116
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,635
Hey. Who is that bastard?

117
00:09:12,469 --> 00:09:13,845
Hurry up and--

118
00:09:13,929 --> 00:09:15,222
You're a dead man!

119
00:09:15,305 --> 00:09:17,182
Damn you!

120
00:09:22,437 --> 00:09:23,605
Damn it!

121
00:09:27,109 --> 00:09:28,986
-Bring it on.
-Stay back!

122
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:42,457
Hey, hurry up!

123
00:09:42,541 --> 00:09:44,001
Starting car wash.

124
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:45,711
-Stop!
-Let's wash up!

125
00:09:45,794 --> 00:09:47,796
-Stop!
-What's going on?

126
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:50,507
-Hey!
-Stop it!

127
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:52,718
-Hey!
-Move!

128
00:09:53,385 --> 00:09:54,928
You little shit!

129
00:09:56,513 --> 00:09:57,639
You little…

130
00:10:00,517 --> 00:10:03,103
Damn it. Hey!

131
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:07,107
-Hey!
-What's going on?

132
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:08,817
-Hey!
-No!

133
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:11,862
-Heads-up!
-Come here, you punk!

134
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,780
-Hey!
-Come here!

135
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:16,116
-Gosh!
-What's going on?

136
00:10:16,199 --> 00:10:17,617
-You bastard!
-Stop!

137
00:10:18,535 --> 00:10:20,537
-Get him!
-Come here!

138
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,706
-You're dead meat!
-Stop!

139
00:10:22,789 --> 00:10:24,708
I'm not the one!

140
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:26,710
-Stop!
-Back off!

141
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:27,794
Where is he?

142
00:10:27,878 --> 00:10:29,212
Over there!

143
00:10:29,296 --> 00:10:30,339
Hey!

144
00:10:31,048 --> 00:10:32,090
He's right there!

145
00:10:49,441 --> 00:10:50,567
Come here!

146
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:00,285
Damn it.

147
00:11:03,789 --> 00:11:04,998
Okay.

148
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:08,502
Get him.

149
00:11:09,211 --> 00:11:10,879
-Hold still.
-Let go of me!

150
00:11:10,962 --> 00:11:12,923
Is this a water park or what?

151
00:11:13,006 --> 00:11:14,883
Where did Jae-hee go
after calling us here?

152
00:11:16,885 --> 00:11:18,387
Stop right there!

153
00:11:19,429 --> 00:11:21,014
Stop coming after me!

154
00:11:21,807 --> 00:11:22,641
Damn it!

155
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:35,487
The chairman gave the order
to the legal department

156
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:38,407
to finalize the succession process
before the shareholder meeting.

157
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,659
Yoon Yi-jun's era at Taekang
is finally beginning.

158
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:41,785
How do you feel?

159
00:11:50,544 --> 00:11:52,629
SECRETARY HAN

160
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,428
There's another message from the Chairman.

161
00:12:00,303 --> 00:12:03,390
He said make sure you quietly take over
without causing any trouble.

162
00:12:05,225 --> 00:12:07,018
Shouldn't you wrap things up?

163
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:09,187
I should.

164
00:12:09,938 --> 00:12:11,857
I'll wrap it up neatly.

165
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:19,990
My goodness.

166
00:12:21,908 --> 00:12:23,743
My leg!

167
00:12:23,827 --> 00:12:25,537
-Damn it!
-Hey!

168
00:12:40,135 --> 00:12:42,012
Aren't you hurt? Are you okay?

169
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:43,763
Do I look okay? Move over!

170
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:53,273
Sorry. Are you okay?

171
00:12:53,982 --> 00:12:55,484
-Let go of me!
-Gosh, that scared me.

172
00:12:56,318 --> 00:12:58,111
My heart skipped a beat there.

173
00:12:58,195 --> 00:12:59,488
He's pretty cool.

174
00:12:59,571 --> 00:13:00,614
Do you know him?

175
00:13:00,697 --> 00:13:02,949
If they're stronger than me,
they're cooler than me.

176
00:13:03,492 --> 00:13:05,994
That goes for guys like Don Lee,
Jung Chan-sung, and him.

177
00:13:06,077 --> 00:13:07,454
-Hey, that--
-Go.

178
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:08,371
What? Okay.

179
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:12,667
Stay down.

180
00:13:27,349 --> 00:13:28,475
EPISODE 1

181
00:13:28,558 --> 00:13:29,976
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

182
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:38,777
MEN'S SHOWER

183
00:13:42,697 --> 00:13:45,408
My goodness! Hey!

184
00:13:45,492 --> 00:13:46,451
You startled me.

185
00:13:46,535 --> 00:13:49,287
I told you to go to the nearby bathhouse!

186
00:13:49,371 --> 00:13:52,207
They won't let me
into the women's locker room.

187
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,667
They'll try to call the cops.

188
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,293
I really want to call the police

189
00:13:55,377 --> 00:13:57,754
to the police agency to have you arrested.

190
00:13:57,837 --> 00:13:59,589
Why are you being so petty?

191
00:13:59,673 --> 00:14:01,007
Can't you wait one minute?

192
00:14:01,091 --> 00:14:02,467
I need one minute to shower!

193
00:14:02,551 --> 00:14:04,844
And when will the women's shower tiles
be replaced?

194
00:14:04,928 --> 00:14:06,763
Why won't you accept my complaint?

195
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:09,349
I don't know!
I don't take care of complaints!

196
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:11,309
You said you'll go on a date this year.

197
00:14:11,393 --> 00:14:12,894
At this rate, it'll be impossible.

198
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:15,105
I'm popular, by the way.

199
00:14:19,943 --> 00:14:22,112
The girls who like you
thinking that you're a boy?

200
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:24,531
Or guys who like you
thinking that you're a boy?

201
00:14:24,614 --> 00:14:26,533
I don't know why they get confused.

202
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:28,785
-It's just you!
-Stop!

203
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:31,371
That's gross. You just wait.

204
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:33,623
Seok-jin, come here quickly.

205
00:14:33,707 --> 00:14:34,749
Hurry up.

206
00:14:37,377 --> 00:14:38,420
Good.

207
00:14:40,171 --> 00:14:41,089
Kim Seok-jin.

208
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:43,675
Our team's one and only mascot and brain.

209
00:14:43,758 --> 00:14:46,052
Be honest with me like a good cop should.

210
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:48,888
When you first saw her

211
00:14:48,972 --> 00:14:50,599
and when you saw her physique,

212
00:14:50,682 --> 00:14:53,101
you thought she was a guy, right?

213
00:14:53,852 --> 00:14:56,605
The more you work with her,
the more you think she's a man.

214
00:14:56,688 --> 00:14:58,023
-Am I right?
-Stop it.

215
00:14:58,106 --> 00:14:59,316
I never thought that.

216
00:15:00,191 --> 00:15:02,694
What? Really?

217
00:15:02,777 --> 00:15:05,405
Hey. Why don't you think
with that clever brain?

218
00:15:06,448 --> 00:15:07,907
-Put some ointment on.
-Okay.

219
00:15:07,991 --> 00:15:09,034
Good work.

220
00:15:21,463 --> 00:15:23,465
-Should I take it to the chairman?
-I'll do it.

221
00:15:23,548 --> 00:15:25,050
I'll go home right after.

222
00:15:25,133 --> 00:15:27,010
-Sir.
-Next time.

223
00:15:31,723 --> 00:15:32,641
Goodbye.

224
00:15:34,434 --> 00:15:36,019
Do you have anything else to report?

225
00:15:36,102 --> 00:15:37,020
No.

226
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:39,105
-It's nothing like that, but…
-Pack up then.

227
00:15:39,189 --> 00:15:41,316
We shouldn't get off work late.

228
00:15:43,151 --> 00:15:44,694
You can get going first.

229
00:15:56,414 --> 00:15:59,376
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

230
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:03,254
Didn't I say we're over?

231
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:05,590
I don't want it to end like this.

232
00:16:05,674 --> 00:16:07,050
I can't do this.

233
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:11,846
You're seriously mistaken.

234
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:16,893
I'm the one who gets to decide
whether we start or end things.

235
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:19,270
-Sir!
-I don't want any loose ends.

236
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:20,814
How much do you want?

237
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:25,652
Do you think I'll back off like this?

238
00:16:25,735 --> 00:16:28,363
I told you to stop clinging.

239
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:31,366
Next time, it won't be just a warning.

240
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,495
What do you mean by that?

241
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:40,291
I don't know.

242
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:45,255
I don't know what I'll do to you
if you decide to take this further.

243
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:07,861
MISSED CALL
SECRETARY HAN

244
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:08,945
I'LL WAIT FOR YOU…

245
00:17:09,988 --> 00:17:11,740
I'll wait for you to come.

246
00:17:11,823 --> 00:17:14,492
If you avoid me again,
I'll go through the secretary's office

247
00:17:14,576 --> 00:17:16,619
and report this to the chairman.

248
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,339
Yoon Yi-jun's era at Taekang
is finally beginning.

249
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:31,968
There's another message from the chairman.

250
00:17:33,178 --> 00:17:36,389
He said make sure you quietly take over
without causing any trouble.

251
00:17:39,601 --> 00:17:41,478
Shouldn't you wrap things up?

252
00:17:41,561 --> 00:17:44,314
TAEKANG GROUP TASK FORCE
MANAGING DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

253
00:17:57,285 --> 00:17:58,244
Yoon Yi-jun.

254
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:36,574
FORENSICS

255
00:18:36,658 --> 00:18:38,701
The victim is a 28-year-old woman.

256
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:41,120
She worked as a secretary
in Taekang's TF team.

257
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:44,707
Cause of death was strangulation,
and based on the ligature marks,

258
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:49,087
the murder weapon was a 100 cm long,
3 cm thick black cowhide belt.

259
00:18:49,963 --> 00:18:53,341
The body and the belt both had
Yoon Yi-jun's fingerprints on them.

260
00:18:54,843 --> 00:18:58,304
What's strange is
that traces of the suspect's DNA,

261
00:18:58,388 --> 00:19:00,932
like skin tissue or blood,
were not found on the victim.

262
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:03,518
However, the victim's fingernails
and right leg show

263
00:19:03,601 --> 00:19:05,520
signs of a struggle.

264
00:19:05,603 --> 00:19:09,190
The culprit is most likely
left-handed or ambidextrous.

265
00:19:09,274 --> 00:19:12,610
The prime suspect is the managing director
of the Taekang TF team,

266
00:19:13,444 --> 00:19:14,487
Yoon Yi-jun.

267
00:19:14,571 --> 00:19:15,613
SUSPECT

268
00:19:15,697 --> 00:19:17,574
YOON YI-JUN, 32-YEAR-OLD, MALE

269
00:19:22,287 --> 00:19:23,329
However,

270
00:19:24,539 --> 00:19:25,957
we couldn't find

271
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:28,084
his motive.

272
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:30,670
So he's denying all allegations.

273
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:32,422
It involved a major conglomerate,

274
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:34,340
so it was assigned to our agency.

275
00:19:35,717 --> 00:19:38,887
But there are rumors going around
in Taekang

276
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:41,431
that Yoon Yi-jun is
a complete piece of work.

277
00:19:43,308 --> 00:19:45,476
Prepare it again.

278
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:46,769
Again!

279
00:19:46,853 --> 00:19:48,855
He disrespects everyone.

280
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:52,692
He flies off the handle
when things don't go his way.

281
00:19:54,319 --> 00:19:56,279
Allegedly, someone passed out
in front of him,

282
00:19:58,990 --> 00:19:59,824
but he laughed.

283
00:20:02,827 --> 00:20:04,787
This is a no-brainer.

284
00:20:05,622 --> 00:20:06,664
They were lovers.

285
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:09,751
He used her for pleasure

286
00:20:10,335 --> 00:20:12,629
and just dumped her.

287
00:20:16,174 --> 00:20:18,426
Han Eun-young was witnessed multiple times

288
00:20:18,509 --> 00:20:20,803
clinging to him, heartbroken.

289
00:20:20,887 --> 00:20:24,933
Wan-gu, just state the facts
instead of using your imagination.

290
00:20:25,016 --> 00:20:27,352
Stop talking about rumors
during the briefing.

291
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:31,272
Come on. There's no smoke without fire.

292
00:20:31,356 --> 00:20:33,650
Those rumors must have started
for a reason.

293
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:37,612
He's a suspect, but why is he
being interviewed as a witness?

294
00:20:37,695 --> 00:20:39,697
He has Taekang's legal department
on his back

295
00:20:39,781 --> 00:20:42,283
and insists that he is innocent.

296
00:20:42,367 --> 00:20:44,160
I said, only state the facts.

297
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:45,912
Don't get Jae-hee riled up.

298
00:20:45,995 --> 00:20:47,622
Hold on. What did you say?

299
00:20:49,791 --> 00:20:54,003
He says that despite the only proof being
none other than his fingerprints?

300
00:20:54,087 --> 00:20:55,129
That's what I'm saying.

301
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:59,175
Yoon Yi-jun is coming tomorrow, right?

302
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:00,718
Yes, he is.

303
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:04,138
Just let me handle it, okay?

304
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:07,475
Yoon Yi-jun or whatever his name is,

305
00:21:08,518 --> 00:21:11,270
I'll punish him with my fist of truth.

306
00:21:12,230 --> 00:21:13,982
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

307
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:32,083
Welcome, sir.

308
00:21:41,009 --> 00:21:43,011
We found a black belt at the scene,

309
00:21:43,094 --> 00:21:45,096
and your fingerprints were found

310
00:21:45,179 --> 00:21:47,890
on the victim's shirt.

311
00:21:47,974 --> 00:21:51,561
As you know, fingerprints
are circumstantial evidence, Detective.

312
00:21:52,145 --> 00:21:53,813
He found Secretary Han

313
00:21:53,896 --> 00:21:56,399
and touched her just to check
if she was okay.

314
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:58,109
Yes, it's circumstantial evidence,

315
00:21:58,192 --> 00:22:00,194
but you should know
that evidence is evidence,

316
00:22:00,278 --> 00:22:02,905
whether it's circumstantial
or direct evidence.

317
00:22:02,989 --> 00:22:05,074
However, when there is no direct evidence,

318
00:22:05,158 --> 00:22:07,493
there were cases
where the suspect was found innocent.

319
00:22:07,577 --> 00:22:09,245
You should know that.

320
00:22:12,832 --> 00:22:14,250
Witness, please answer yourself.

321
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:16,085
Will you keep acting like this?

322
00:22:41,611 --> 00:22:45,239
Based on the direction
of the signs of a struggle

323
00:22:45,323 --> 00:22:48,618
and the direction of the belt marks,
the culprit is likely left-handed.

324
00:22:48,701 --> 00:22:49,535
You're left-handed.

325
00:22:51,037 --> 00:22:53,623
Is there anything you'd like to say?

326
00:22:59,003 --> 00:23:01,380
I'm the only person
whose fingerprints were found,

327
00:23:01,464 --> 00:23:03,424
and I'm left-handed too.

328
00:23:03,508 --> 00:23:05,968
So all the evidence points to me.

329
00:23:07,762 --> 00:23:09,514
This is quite the predicament.

330
00:23:13,643 --> 00:23:15,019
So, Detective,

331
00:23:17,271 --> 00:23:18,815
do you really think

332
00:23:20,024 --> 00:23:23,569
I murdered Secretary Han?

333
00:23:24,654 --> 00:23:26,697
Yes! You're the one who killed her!

334
00:23:28,783 --> 00:23:30,076
Where did Kang go?

335
00:23:30,785 --> 00:23:32,745
She wanted to punish him with her fists.

336
00:23:32,829 --> 00:23:34,914
-She's out on duty.
-What?

337
00:23:35,998 --> 00:23:38,000
It's a voice phishing awareness seminar.

338
00:23:40,670 --> 00:23:42,713
Her sense of justice may cause trouble,

339
00:23:43,381 --> 00:23:45,216
so I guess the captain got ahead of her.

340
00:23:46,259 --> 00:23:48,719
Gosh, you eat so well.

341
00:23:48,803 --> 00:23:50,012
Thank you for the meal.

342
00:23:50,096 --> 00:23:51,139
I'll get going.

343
00:23:51,722 --> 00:23:52,640
Have some more meat.

344
00:23:53,391 --> 00:23:54,308
You want more rice?

345
00:23:54,392 --> 00:23:56,435
No, it's fine. I had enough.

346
00:23:56,519 --> 00:23:58,813
Wait! What do you mean "enough"?

347
00:23:58,896 --> 00:24:01,357
-Goodness, here. Have some more.
-Have more.

348
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:04,777
-Gosh, voice phishing is so scary.
-The food is so good.

349
00:24:06,154 --> 00:24:09,031
Fine, I get it. According to the records,

350
00:24:09,115 --> 00:24:10,324
on the day of the incident,

351
00:24:10,408 --> 00:24:13,828
the CCTV camera on the 32nd floor
was under maintenance.

352
00:24:13,911 --> 00:24:16,789
I heard the maintenance date
was known to everyone.

353
00:24:16,873 --> 00:24:19,959
You must've known
that the camera wasn't working.

354
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:22,420
I'm not sure.

355
00:24:23,421 --> 00:24:24,839
I was on a business trip.

356
00:24:29,844 --> 00:24:32,263
There was a record of
you leaving the office at 21:10,

357
00:24:32,346 --> 00:24:34,348
but why did you come back to the office?

358
00:24:35,099 --> 00:24:37,018
She said she'd wait for me
until I arrived.

359
00:24:37,894 --> 00:24:39,520
If she doesn't go home because of me,

360
00:24:40,938 --> 00:24:42,523
I become a bad boss.

361
00:24:46,027 --> 00:24:49,155
Were you in a romantic relationship
with the victim?

362
00:24:49,238 --> 00:24:50,531
Is the rumor true?

363
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:53,784
Don't tell me…

364
00:24:54,827 --> 00:24:58,539
Did Secretary Han like me?

365
00:25:00,041 --> 00:25:01,042
Witness.

366
00:25:03,127 --> 00:25:06,088
If you keep this up,
we cannot confirm anything.

367
00:25:06,172 --> 00:25:09,508
He has the right
not to answer your questions.

368
00:25:09,592 --> 00:25:12,053
We have the right to exclude you
if you keep interfering.

369
00:25:12,136 --> 00:25:15,473
You need to stop asking
these clearly loaded questions, Detective.

370
00:25:16,182 --> 00:25:18,601
Please note that he's been cooperating

371
00:25:18,684 --> 00:25:21,270
despite being treated
like a murder suspect.

372
00:25:21,354 --> 00:25:22,480
Also,

373
00:25:23,231 --> 00:25:25,316
you have no right to exclude me.

374
00:25:26,025 --> 00:25:26,901
Who the hell is--

375
00:25:33,532 --> 00:25:34,742
Have you lost your mind?

376
00:25:35,743 --> 00:25:36,702
I'm so full.

377
00:25:40,623 --> 00:25:41,791
-Salute.
-Hey.

378
00:25:48,381 --> 00:25:50,675
Thank you for your cooperation, Mr. Yoon.

379
00:25:51,717 --> 00:25:53,678
Please investigate thoroughly

380
00:25:54,387 --> 00:25:55,554
and properly.

381
00:25:56,138 --> 00:25:57,890
Yes, sir. Come this way.

382
00:26:01,602 --> 00:26:02,728
Properly.

383
00:26:06,357 --> 00:26:07,817
Damn it.

384
00:26:26,502 --> 00:26:29,088
How dare you summon
the successor of Taekang without notice?

385
00:26:31,757 --> 00:26:32,591
Sir.

386
00:26:33,426 --> 00:26:36,679
You admit that Yoon Yi-jun is
the prime suspect, right?

387
00:26:38,848 --> 00:26:40,057
Captain Park.

388
00:26:40,141 --> 00:26:43,436
Why do you think
this case has been assigned to your team?

389
00:26:44,854 --> 00:26:46,856
You are understaffed,

390
00:26:46,939 --> 00:26:49,150
you are short on results,

391
00:26:49,233 --> 00:26:51,444
you lack skills,

392
00:26:51,527 --> 00:26:52,945
and you even lack good looks!

393
00:26:53,904 --> 00:26:55,990
The only thing you're doing too much of

394
00:26:56,073 --> 00:26:58,326
is causing trouble.

395
00:26:58,409 --> 00:27:01,704
But I was being generous with you guys
by giving you this case!

396
00:27:06,167 --> 00:27:08,502
According to the circumstances,
she took her own life.

397
00:27:09,962 --> 00:27:11,172
Is this hard to understand?

398
00:27:17,178 --> 00:27:20,514
Stop going around causing trouble.

399
00:27:21,474 --> 00:27:24,268
Assess who you are going up against
before you fight them.

400
00:27:25,394 --> 00:27:26,437
Okay?

401
00:27:30,816 --> 00:27:32,068
Captain.

402
00:27:32,651 --> 00:27:35,446
Are we letting another guy
get away with it because he's rich?

403
00:27:35,529 --> 00:27:37,406
We can't end the investigation like this.

404
00:27:37,490 --> 00:27:40,117
Didn't you hear?
We have no direct evidence.

405
00:27:40,701 --> 00:27:43,162
-Damn it.
-Jeez.

406
00:27:43,245 --> 00:27:44,830
What can we do even if we catch him?

407
00:27:44,914 --> 00:27:47,375
Even the country's president
can't mess with Taekang.

408
00:27:48,084 --> 00:27:48,918
Goodness.

409
00:27:49,835 --> 00:27:52,004
This is a blow to our pride.

410
00:27:52,088 --> 00:27:55,341
We have pride. We just don't have money.

411
00:27:55,424 --> 00:27:59,845
Seriously!
Can you just lend me 180,000 won?

412
00:27:59,929 --> 00:28:01,555
Sorry, everyone.

413
00:28:02,056 --> 00:28:02,890
Quiet down.

414
00:28:02,973 --> 00:28:05,142
The rich weasel their way out
of everything.

415
00:28:06,143 --> 00:28:07,144
It's so unfair!

416
00:28:08,646 --> 00:28:10,689
-Let's have a drink.
-Not you. Put it down.

417
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:13,734
-Put it down.
-Come on.

418
00:28:19,907 --> 00:28:21,992
-Come on. Just this once.
-Jeez.

419
00:28:22,076 --> 00:28:25,371
Captain, just one glass.

420
00:28:25,955 --> 00:28:28,499
-Jeez.
-Man.

421
00:28:28,582 --> 00:28:29,583
Let's drink.

422
00:28:29,667 --> 00:28:30,918
Whatever.

423
00:28:31,877 --> 00:28:34,713
Hey, she's drinking it all!

424
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:40,636
Sir, I'm here.

425
00:28:45,307 --> 00:28:48,269
Undercover investigation
isn't as easy as it sounds.

426
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:50,020
I'll get going.

427
00:28:50,104 --> 00:28:51,730
Back in the day…

428
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:55,109
Why is my mouth so dry?

429
00:28:59,321 --> 00:29:00,322
Kang Jae-hee!

430
00:29:02,283 --> 00:29:04,076
I knew she'd run off.

431
00:29:05,286 --> 00:29:06,787
What are you doing? Go after her.

432
00:29:06,871 --> 00:29:08,956
Detective Kim went.

433
00:29:09,915 --> 00:29:10,875
Damn you.

434
00:29:10,958 --> 00:29:13,169
Wait for me! Jeez.

435
00:29:19,341 --> 00:29:21,760
Why does she do that
every time she drinks?

436
00:29:21,844 --> 00:29:24,096
That little brat

437
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:28,142
lost something very precious to her
because of a moment's hesitation.

438
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:29,768
That's why

439
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:33,522
she obnoxiously acts like that
whenever she drinks.

440
00:29:33,606 --> 00:29:35,941
Goodness, I feel bad for her.

441
00:29:39,069 --> 00:29:41,030
-What do I owe you?
-It's 184,000 won.

442
00:29:42,490 --> 00:29:44,074
That damn 180,000 won.

443
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,535
You thought you could get away?

444
00:29:46,619 --> 00:29:48,037
-What are you doing?
-Get off!

445
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:49,246
-Jae-hee!
-Let me go.

446
00:29:49,330 --> 00:29:51,081
-Get off!
-Goodness.

447
00:29:51,165 --> 00:29:52,374
-Get off!
-Cut it out.

448
00:29:53,083 --> 00:29:54,418
Sorry.

449
00:29:55,294 --> 00:29:57,379
-You'll hurt yourself.
-Sir.

450
00:29:57,463 --> 00:30:00,174
Why are you holding me? He's running away!

451
00:30:00,758 --> 00:30:02,593
-What are you doing?
-Hey, arrest her.

452
00:30:04,261 --> 00:30:05,429
Why are you arresting me?

453
00:30:05,513 --> 00:30:08,474
I didn't commit any crimes!

454
00:30:08,557 --> 00:30:09,767
You just committed

455
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:11,352
the crime of making me run.

456
00:30:11,435 --> 00:30:13,604
-Damn it.
-Guilty as charged.

457
00:30:13,687 --> 00:30:14,772
-Come on.
-Let's go.

458
00:30:14,855 --> 00:30:16,023
Where? I'm not going!

459
00:30:16,106 --> 00:30:17,399
I need to catch him!

460
00:30:17,483 --> 00:30:18,776
I'm not going!

461
00:30:18,859 --> 00:30:20,486
Come on.

462
00:30:32,706 --> 00:30:34,833
The police will quietly bury this case.

463
00:30:35,417 --> 00:30:36,710
The chairman has made a move.

464
00:30:36,794 --> 00:30:40,172
He won't let any controversy slide
with the shareholder meeting coming up.

465
00:30:43,717 --> 00:30:45,594
If only Secretary Han
didn't get wind of it…

466
00:30:47,513 --> 00:30:49,390
All eyes will be on you for a while.

467
00:30:50,516 --> 00:30:51,892
Things got complicated.

468
00:30:51,976 --> 00:30:54,937
You need to lie low
if you want to lower the risks.

469
00:30:57,773 --> 00:30:58,732
How exciting.

470
00:30:59,358 --> 00:31:01,735
Everyone will be excited to see me.

471
00:31:36,061 --> 00:31:39,690
TAEKANG, A $2.2 BILLION
SAUDI PLANT CONTRACT

472
00:31:39,773 --> 00:31:41,442
How smug.

473
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:43,527
YOON MAKES BOLD MOVES IN SAUDI…

474
00:31:45,571 --> 00:31:48,032
TAEKANG YOON YI-JUN

475
00:31:48,115 --> 00:31:48,991
YOON YI-JUN

476
00:31:49,074 --> 00:31:52,036
YOON YI-JUN SIGNALS
A NEW GENERATION OF LEADERSHIP IN TAEKANG?

477
00:31:52,119 --> 00:31:55,539
How much must they have paid people off
to keep the case under wraps?

478
00:31:57,875 --> 00:32:01,211
YOON YI-JUN'S SECRETARY

479
00:32:01,295 --> 00:32:02,671
BECOMING A SECRETARY

480
00:32:02,755 --> 00:32:04,882
TAEKANG GROUP,
RECRUITING TF TEAM SECRETARY

481
00:32:40,417 --> 00:32:42,294
Are you feeling sick?

482
00:32:42,378 --> 00:32:44,380
When are you coming to work?

483
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:47,091
I'm lonely.

484
00:32:47,174 --> 00:32:49,343
No one's at the office,
including you and Han…

485
00:32:53,889 --> 00:32:56,308
If you're lonely, you can hug Jerry.

486
00:32:56,850 --> 00:33:01,063
Before that, the lighting
should be set to exactly 400.

487
00:33:01,146 --> 00:33:02,106
Sir?

488
00:33:02,189 --> 00:33:06,443
I'd like to get the sunlight evenly.

489
00:33:11,407 --> 00:33:12,616
Get lost.

490
00:33:15,619 --> 00:33:17,287
What are we going to do now?

491
00:33:21,166 --> 00:33:22,292
-Hello.
-Hey.

492
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:30,759
Our captain is

493
00:33:32,302 --> 00:33:33,595
always sleeping.

494
00:33:37,766 --> 00:33:38,726
Good morning.

495
00:33:39,685 --> 00:33:42,062
-Good morning.
-You rotten brat.

496
00:33:47,234 --> 00:33:48,819
What? Who's this for?

497
00:33:50,195 --> 00:33:51,071
Sir.

498
00:33:57,161 --> 00:33:57,995
YOON YI-JUN KILLED HER

499
00:34:01,415 --> 00:34:03,584
I told you to stop clinging.

500
00:34:04,084 --> 00:34:05,961
Next time, it won't be just a warning.

501
00:34:08,130 --> 00:34:09,256
What do you mean by that?

502
00:34:12,718 --> 00:34:13,802
I don't know.

503
00:34:14,470 --> 00:34:18,766
I don't know what I'll do to you
if you decide to take this further.

504
00:34:21,685 --> 00:34:23,604
I guess they really were
seeing each other.

505
00:34:26,023 --> 00:34:27,816
Where are Jung Wan-gu and Kim Seok-jin?

506
00:34:27,900 --> 00:34:30,402
They went to meet the victim's family
for the last time.

507
00:34:30,486 --> 00:34:31,945
-Tell them to come back.
-Okay.

508
00:34:36,950 --> 00:34:38,285
I apologize for this.

509
00:34:39,411 --> 00:34:40,829
You're saying the deceased

510
00:34:41,705 --> 00:34:43,499
didn't show any strange behaviors

511
00:34:43,582 --> 00:34:46,418
or receive any suspicious text messages?

512
00:34:47,127 --> 00:34:48,879
Even if it seems insignificant,

513
00:34:48,962 --> 00:34:52,007
please let us know if you recall anything.

514
00:34:52,674 --> 00:34:55,761
Why was your sister receiving
your phone bill at her address?

515
00:34:57,721 --> 00:34:59,389
My sister used that phone.

516
00:35:00,557 --> 00:35:01,850
It was just under my name.

517
00:35:02,434 --> 00:35:05,479
What? Han Eun-young used two phones?

518
00:35:09,817 --> 00:35:12,236
So there's another phone
that looks like that?

519
00:35:12,319 --> 00:35:13,403
Yes, sir.

520
00:35:14,238 --> 00:35:15,405
What happened?

521
00:35:15,489 --> 00:35:18,575
We tracked its final location,
and it was near Yoon Yi-jun's office.

522
00:35:21,286 --> 00:35:24,623
The only phone we found
was her work phone.

523
00:35:25,207 --> 00:35:26,625
So where is that phone?

524
00:35:26,708 --> 00:35:29,503
According to the victim's family,
someone likely hid it.

525
00:35:30,671 --> 00:35:33,674
If we can find the phone,
we'll have direct evidence.

526
00:35:34,258 --> 00:35:38,262
Right. Whether or not Han Eun-young
and Yoon Yi-jun were lovers,

527
00:35:38,345 --> 00:35:40,681
there's definitely something
on that phone.

528
00:35:40,764 --> 00:35:41,974
TAEKANG SMARTPHONE K22 MEGA BLACK

529
00:35:42,057 --> 00:35:43,058
What I'm saying is,

530
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:45,269
we have to look for the lost phone first.

531
00:35:45,352 --> 00:35:47,813
We can get a warrant to search Taekang--

532
00:35:47,896 --> 00:35:51,233
We won't be able to find the phone,
the proof, or the culprit like that.

533
00:35:51,900 --> 00:35:54,570
The higher-ups are telling us
to bury this case,

534
00:35:54,653 --> 00:35:56,488
and Taekang is playing dumb.

535
00:35:56,572 --> 00:35:58,031
What choice do we have?

536
00:35:58,115 --> 00:35:59,491
We have to find it.

537
00:35:59,575 --> 00:36:00,909
Where the hell are these guys?

538
00:36:01,952 --> 00:36:02,870
Hide everything!

539
00:36:02,953 --> 00:36:03,954
Hide them!

540
00:36:12,462 --> 00:36:13,505
What are you doing?

541
00:36:13,589 --> 00:36:15,632
We were in a meeting.

542
00:36:15,716 --> 00:36:16,758
What meeting?

543
00:36:18,302 --> 00:36:19,970
-Spit it out.
-Sir?

544
00:36:21,847 --> 00:36:23,682
The meeting was about

545
00:36:24,391 --> 00:36:25,851
whether we should

546
00:36:26,643 --> 00:36:30,105
have dinner delivered or not.

547
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:33,025
How about hamburgers?
They have the perfect nutritional balance.

548
00:36:33,108 --> 00:36:34,902
Make them double cheeseburgers!

549
00:36:34,985 --> 00:36:36,904
-Is this the hamburger place?
-Not so fast.

550
00:36:38,113 --> 00:36:39,823
Would you like to join us?

551
00:36:39,907 --> 00:36:41,450
Enough of this bullshit.

552
00:36:41,533 --> 00:36:43,577
You're all such hard workers.

553
00:36:43,660 --> 00:36:46,622
Why aren't you submitting
the report on the Taekang Case?

554
00:36:46,705 --> 00:36:48,040
What's wrong?

555
00:36:48,123 --> 00:36:49,666
Does it piss you off

556
00:36:49,750 --> 00:36:52,294
that someone below your class
is bossing you around?

557
00:36:52,377 --> 00:36:53,253
Is that why?

558
00:36:55,297 --> 00:36:57,090
If I felt pissed off,

559
00:36:57,174 --> 00:36:59,718
I would've worked hard to get promoted.

560
00:37:01,303 --> 00:37:03,513
-Sir.
-Jeez, you fools.

561
00:37:04,973 --> 00:37:06,224
Submit the report today.

562
00:37:10,145 --> 00:37:12,189
The victim's family is pretty resistant.

563
00:37:12,940 --> 00:37:15,442
If we brush off a tycoon case like this,

564
00:37:15,525 --> 00:37:18,445
someone will leak this
as a shoddy investigation to the press,

565
00:37:18,528 --> 00:37:20,572
and the police will
get stoned by the public.

566
00:37:20,656 --> 00:37:22,240
We need a valid excuse

567
00:37:22,324 --> 00:37:23,825
to justify our actions, you know.

568
00:37:23,909 --> 00:37:26,995
While we're on the subject,
just order some hot stone pot rice.

569
00:37:27,079 --> 00:37:28,747
-Is this a Korean restaurant?
-Shut up!

570
00:37:30,791 --> 00:37:33,335
-Whatever.
-Do as you please until the deadline.

571
00:37:33,418 --> 00:37:34,670
What?

572
00:37:35,128 --> 00:37:36,129
If you find nothing,

573
00:37:37,047 --> 00:37:38,215
you'll all pay for it.

574
00:37:39,341 --> 00:37:40,842
-Got that?
-Yes, sir.

575
00:37:42,177 --> 00:37:45,055
You really are a ridiculous bunch.

576
00:37:51,937 --> 00:37:53,230
No way.

577
00:37:53,313 --> 00:37:54,648
We don't have time.

578
00:37:55,565 --> 00:37:56,525
Any good ideas?

579
00:38:00,988 --> 00:38:02,489
I have one.

580
00:38:04,157 --> 00:38:06,118
They're looking for a personal secretary.

581
00:38:06,868 --> 00:38:08,328
Look at this, Captain.

582
00:38:08,412 --> 00:38:09,955
Taekang's TF team.

583
00:38:10,038 --> 00:38:12,499
That's the team
where Yoon Yi-jun is a managing director.

584
00:38:12,582 --> 00:38:15,377
The job description says
secretarial and bodyguard work.

585
00:38:15,460 --> 00:38:19,506
Qualifications include martial arts
and security experience.

586
00:38:19,589 --> 00:38:22,801
If I become the secretary,
I can investigate him up close like this.

587
00:38:22,884 --> 00:38:24,886
-What do you think?
-Jeez.

588
00:38:24,970 --> 00:38:28,181
Back off already.
You're making me feel ill.

589
00:38:28,265 --> 00:38:30,100
-Can you do something with her?
-No.

590
00:38:30,183 --> 00:38:31,810
Han Eun-young's lost phone.

591
00:38:32,436 --> 00:38:35,939
It's an item we must find.

592
00:38:36,481 --> 00:38:39,317
Currently, Yoon Yi-jun
most likely hid it somewhere.

593
00:38:39,401 --> 00:38:42,571
But Taekang built a wall around him.

594
00:38:42,654 --> 00:38:43,697
A direct approach?

595
00:38:44,364 --> 00:38:46,366
It won't be easy. Don't you agree?

596
00:38:46,950 --> 00:38:49,786
-I agree.
-We all know.

597
00:38:49,870 --> 00:38:52,080
But he knows all our faces
from the investigation.

598
00:38:52,789 --> 00:38:53,957
Not all our faces.

599
00:38:56,209 --> 00:38:57,294
We have one left.

600
00:39:07,012 --> 00:39:09,264
They're looking for a male secretary.

601
00:39:09,765 --> 00:39:10,599
A male secretary…

602
00:39:14,269 --> 00:39:15,228
MAN

603
00:39:18,940 --> 00:39:19,858
A man!

604
00:39:21,735 --> 00:39:24,821
People think I'm a man all the time.

605
00:39:24,905 --> 00:39:26,573
Even though

606
00:39:26,656 --> 00:39:28,241
I'm just being who I am.

607
00:39:28,325 --> 00:39:32,746
I will be a man for real this time!

608
00:39:32,829 --> 00:39:34,372
Can we do something about her?

609
00:39:34,456 --> 00:39:37,334
Arrest her and put her behind bars.
She's so loud.

610
00:39:38,919 --> 00:39:39,795
Bravo!

611
00:39:40,879 --> 00:39:42,881
-This can work.
-What's with you?

612
00:39:42,964 --> 00:39:46,259
I mean, she's had experience
fighting men before.

613
00:39:50,555 --> 00:39:51,807
What the hell?

614
00:39:52,641 --> 00:39:55,685
Hey. You're 3885, right?

615
00:40:09,366 --> 00:40:10,700
I'll let you live.

616
00:40:13,245 --> 00:40:16,164
What good weather to arrest them.

617
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:23,839
Do you know who I am?

618
00:40:25,173 --> 00:40:30,554
I'm Kang Jae-hee
from the Violent Crimes Unit!

619
00:40:32,097 --> 00:40:34,307
This is going to work for sure.

620
00:40:34,391 --> 00:40:35,642
I'm certain!

621
00:40:35,725 --> 00:40:37,519
She'll be next to him all the time.

622
00:40:37,978 --> 00:40:39,980
He won't be fooled by her.

623
00:40:41,022 --> 00:40:43,316
Excuse me. Here's your stew.

624
00:40:47,237 --> 00:40:50,949
I heard something funny
from the lady in the kitchen.

625
00:40:51,032 --> 00:40:52,826
Are you a girl, Detective?

626
00:40:53,910 --> 00:40:55,412
Yes, I am.

627
00:40:55,495 --> 00:40:57,706
-Why state the obvious?
-My word.

628
00:40:57,789 --> 00:41:00,250
I saw you for three years,
but I didn't notice at all.

629
00:41:00,834 --> 00:41:04,462
I thought she was a man
because she looked so manly and reliable.

630
00:41:04,546 --> 00:41:05,672
I know.

631
00:41:06,715 --> 00:41:07,757
Well?

632
00:41:07,841 --> 00:41:09,718
I'm telling you, this could work.

633
00:41:11,469 --> 00:41:14,723
Are you convinced that
Yoon Yi-jun can be tricked as well now?

634
00:41:14,806 --> 00:41:18,435
Being a secretary there
isn't about being good at martial arts.

635
00:41:18,518 --> 00:41:21,271
Do you even know how to be a secretary?

636
00:41:21,354 --> 00:41:23,106
Well, that can…

637
00:41:23,190 --> 00:41:25,358
That's for
after she passes the initial screening.

638
00:41:26,359 --> 00:41:27,444
I'll help her.

639
00:41:29,321 --> 00:41:30,822
-You will?
-You will?

640
00:41:39,331 --> 00:41:40,582
It's over if you fail.

641
00:41:40,665 --> 00:41:44,461
Yes, sir! I'll begin by writing a resume.

642
00:41:45,253 --> 00:41:46,087
Thank you, sir!

643
00:41:49,007 --> 00:41:50,550
You're dead meat.

644
00:41:59,559 --> 00:42:00,644
Mom.

645
00:42:01,269 --> 00:42:02,687
Mom.

646
00:42:02,771 --> 00:42:04,231
Mom, wake up.

647
00:42:27,587 --> 00:42:28,838
What are you doing?

648
00:42:32,884 --> 00:42:35,136
The E is missing.
Are you admiring the painting?

649
00:42:38,723 --> 00:42:40,600
It's tilted more to the left
than yesterday.

650
00:42:40,684 --> 00:42:42,978
It's due to an external force.

651
00:42:44,729 --> 00:42:46,940
Where are you saying it's tilted?

652
00:42:49,401 --> 00:42:50,652
Did you not sleep yesterday?

653
00:42:51,152 --> 00:42:53,029
And what's with hiring a new secretary?

654
00:42:53,113 --> 00:42:53,989
Sir.

655
00:42:54,739 --> 00:42:55,907
Secretary Jung.

656
00:42:57,409 --> 00:42:58,493
Welcome.

657
00:42:59,119 --> 00:43:00,161
This is not right.

658
00:43:00,870 --> 00:43:02,789
You don't care
about degrees and credentials?

659
00:43:03,748 --> 00:43:04,708
You're right.

660
00:43:05,208 --> 00:43:08,003
You graduated from a great school,
Secretary Jang.

661
00:43:08,086 --> 00:43:09,587
-Hey, it's…
-It's Jung.

662
00:43:10,672 --> 00:43:13,925
Book-smart ones waste time thinking,
even when danger hits.

663
00:43:14,467 --> 00:43:16,011
I'll filter them out and hire

664
00:43:16,094 --> 00:43:18,096
only black belts
or experienced bodyguards.

665
00:43:18,179 --> 00:43:19,848
What about the secretarial work?

666
00:43:19,931 --> 00:43:23,059
I'm using
all my energy to do all the work.

667
00:43:25,020 --> 00:43:25,854
Look.

668
00:43:25,937 --> 00:43:26,813
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

669
00:43:26,896 --> 00:43:29,107
I can't put up with this anymore.

670
00:43:29,816 --> 00:43:31,484
Gosh, Secretary Jung.

671
00:43:31,568 --> 00:43:33,403
You need to calm down first.

672
00:43:33,486 --> 00:43:34,612
Don't stop me.

673
00:43:34,696 --> 00:43:36,031
You can quit if you want.

674
00:43:36,531 --> 00:43:37,991
It's none of my business.

675
00:43:38,074 --> 00:43:39,659
Yes, I will.

676
00:43:39,743 --> 00:43:43,079
Make sure you properly hand off,
Secretary Choi.

677
00:43:43,163 --> 00:43:45,123
I'm Secretary Jung.

678
00:43:45,206 --> 00:43:47,834
Right, Secretary Jung.

679
00:43:47,917 --> 00:43:49,836
I know your name. I do!

680
00:43:52,797 --> 00:43:54,841
Disqualified due to too many credentials.

681
00:43:54,924 --> 00:43:56,259
Disqualified!

682
00:43:57,260 --> 00:43:58,386
Everyone is disqualified.

683
00:44:06,644 --> 00:44:09,856
Judo, hapkido, and taekwondo.
Adds up to a ninth-dan black belt.

684
00:44:10,690 --> 00:44:12,359
He has the looks,

685
00:44:12,442 --> 00:44:14,319
but he has zero experience as a secretary.

686
00:44:16,404 --> 00:44:19,532
I hope he meets a clueless secretary

687
00:44:19,616 --> 00:44:21,659
and goes through a tough time.

688
00:44:21,743 --> 00:44:24,079
Then he'll realize that I was great.

689
00:44:24,579 --> 00:44:27,374
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

690
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:29,667
I got in.

691
00:44:30,668 --> 00:44:31,586
Hey, Kang!

692
00:44:33,421 --> 00:44:35,924
-Give it to me.
-I can't believe this worked.

693
00:44:37,926 --> 00:44:38,802
-Nice!
-Nice!

694
00:44:38,885 --> 00:44:39,886
TAEKANG GROUP: APPLICATION RESULTS

695
00:44:39,969 --> 00:44:42,847
See? I said
you'd get into Taekang no problem.

696
00:44:42,931 --> 00:44:44,891
I knew this would happen.

697
00:44:45,433 --> 00:44:46,935
Don't just stand around.

698
00:44:47,811 --> 00:44:48,978
Prepare for the interview.

699
00:44:49,062 --> 00:44:50,855
-Yes, sir!
-At ease.

700
00:44:53,066 --> 00:44:54,609
You need to make a good impression.

701
00:44:55,902 --> 00:44:57,112
Look confident.

702
00:44:57,195 --> 00:44:58,863
Though he first reported the crime,

703
00:44:58,947 --> 00:44:59,864
he's still a suspect.

704
00:45:00,365 --> 00:45:01,241
Next…

705
00:45:03,451 --> 00:45:04,702
Hold this one up.

706
00:45:06,246 --> 00:45:07,664
This one suits you the best.

707
00:45:10,959 --> 00:45:12,544
REPUBLIC OF KOREA ARMY
KANG JAE-HEE

708
00:45:31,563 --> 00:45:33,064
All right, Kang Jae-hee.

709
00:45:33,148 --> 00:45:34,941
Interviews are all about confidence.

710
00:45:35,733 --> 00:45:36,943
Let's go.

711
00:45:54,252 --> 00:45:58,590
"I will give him support by his side
so the managing director can…"

712
00:45:58,673 --> 00:46:00,508
"I will give him support by his side…"

713
00:46:02,677 --> 00:46:03,970
What kind of a place is this?

714
00:46:04,053 --> 00:46:05,180
What's going on?

715
00:46:05,263 --> 00:46:06,264
REJECTED

716
00:46:07,974 --> 00:46:09,267
REJECTED

717
00:46:10,935 --> 00:46:12,520
Mom, this place is weird.

718
00:46:12,604 --> 00:46:13,730
-So weird.
-Weird?

719
00:46:14,314 --> 00:46:15,148
Weird?

720
00:46:18,234 --> 00:46:19,277
How is it going?

721
00:46:19,903 --> 00:46:22,197
This place is a bit weird.

722
00:46:22,280 --> 00:46:23,573
Candidate Ten, Kang Jae-hee.

723
00:46:23,656 --> 00:46:25,408
Please get ready.

724
00:46:25,492 --> 00:46:26,618
Okay.

725
00:46:33,917 --> 00:46:35,293
Please come in, Kang Jae-hee.

726
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:42,467
FORMER SPECIAL FORCES

727
00:46:43,051 --> 00:46:46,471
"This place is a bit weird"?

728
00:46:46,554 --> 00:46:47,764
THIS PLACE… IS A BIT WEIRD…

729
00:46:47,847 --> 00:46:49,307
It is really weird.

730
00:46:49,807 --> 00:46:52,644
Why would a simpleton like her
sound so serious?

731
00:46:53,478 --> 00:46:55,897
Let's see what happens.
She's qualified enough.

732
00:46:55,980 --> 00:46:57,273
And we've prepared hard.

733
00:47:05,114 --> 00:47:08,117
Hello, I'm Candidate Ten, Kang Jae-hee.

734
00:47:45,863 --> 00:47:47,407
What's with him? What a lunatic.

735
00:47:48,616 --> 00:47:49,784
I won.

736
00:47:50,493 --> 00:47:51,661
What's with his tone?

737
00:47:55,540 --> 00:47:56,499
Former special forces?

738
00:47:56,583 --> 00:47:58,501
-Yes, sir.
-No wonder,

739
00:47:58,585 --> 00:48:00,128
your posture is sharp.

740
00:48:04,257 --> 00:48:05,425
Look at the photo

741
00:48:05,508 --> 00:48:08,011
and identify three things
that differ from reality.

742
00:48:16,144 --> 00:48:17,061
You may start.

743
00:48:45,131 --> 00:48:49,385
-Crap, I'm screwed.
-Thank you for coming. You may leave.

744
00:48:50,803 --> 00:48:51,804
I found two.

745
00:48:51,888 --> 00:48:54,223
Is that so?

746
00:48:54,891 --> 00:48:56,601
What did you find?

747
00:48:56,684 --> 00:48:58,895
The document on the table.
The graph has changed.

748
00:48:59,646 --> 00:49:02,899
The angle of the globe
has been tilted 15 degrees to the left.

749
00:49:13,618 --> 00:49:16,704
If you don't mind,
may I ask what the last one is?

750
00:49:18,831 --> 00:49:19,749
There is none.

751
00:49:21,876 --> 00:49:23,169
It was two to begin with.

752
00:49:25,338 --> 00:49:27,006
But if I say three,

753
00:49:27,090 --> 00:49:30,468
people try hard to look for the third one.
It's fun watching them struggle.

754
00:49:32,595 --> 00:49:34,555
So you're observant.

755
00:49:34,639 --> 00:49:37,934
They say the special forces get assigned
top-secret missions.

756
00:49:38,643 --> 00:49:40,186
Have you ever killed anyone?

757
00:49:41,979 --> 00:49:42,814
Sir?

758
00:49:44,482 --> 00:49:45,817
Have you killed anyone before?

759
00:49:49,654 --> 00:49:52,699
I've been invested in that area
these days.

760
00:49:55,493 --> 00:49:58,746
Is your current interest murdering people?

761
00:50:35,700 --> 00:50:37,034
Did you kill Han Eun-young?

762
00:50:52,842 --> 00:50:55,303
I like your boldness,
daydreaming during an interview.

763
00:50:55,386 --> 00:50:56,721
So what's your answer?

764
00:51:00,099 --> 00:51:01,392
So you haven't killed anyone?

765
00:51:03,478 --> 00:51:04,979
I've witnessed a murder before.

766
00:51:07,315 --> 00:51:08,649
What kind of situation was it?

767
00:51:08,733 --> 00:51:11,110
You get extra points for being honest.

768
00:51:18,284 --> 00:51:20,787
It was a hostage rescue operation,
and the person who died

769
00:51:22,038 --> 00:51:23,080
was my comrade.

770
00:51:23,748 --> 00:51:24,874
Kang Jae-hee!

771
00:51:25,625 --> 00:51:27,084
Have mercy on me.

772
00:51:30,713 --> 00:51:33,174
Sergeant Go!

773
00:51:33,257 --> 00:51:35,301
No!

774
00:51:41,224 --> 00:51:44,685
It came down to a split second
between life and death.

775
00:51:44,769 --> 00:51:46,437
If you didn't hesitate,

776
00:51:46,521 --> 00:51:49,607
your comrade would've lived.

777
00:51:52,026 --> 00:51:54,445
So did you catch the bastard?

778
00:51:54,529 --> 00:51:56,113
The one who killed your comrade?

779
00:52:03,996 --> 00:52:05,122
I guess you didn't.

780
00:52:07,250 --> 00:52:11,087
He must be living it up somewhere
after killing your comrade.

781
00:52:14,215 --> 00:52:16,884
Let's try something fun.
Take five steps back.

782
00:52:20,221 --> 00:52:23,015
Now, let's imagine this.

783
00:52:23,099 --> 00:52:25,852
What would you do if you saw that scumbag?

784
00:52:29,313 --> 00:52:31,649
He's approaching you
from five meters away.

785
00:52:31,732 --> 00:52:34,277
Three meters. He locks eyes with you.

786
00:52:34,360 --> 00:52:38,114
Two meters. The jerk remembers you
and your fallen comrade.

787
00:52:38,197 --> 00:52:39,448
One meter.

788
00:52:39,532 --> 00:52:40,908
He smiles at you.

789
00:52:40,992 --> 00:52:42,910
Zero meters.

790
00:52:56,632 --> 00:53:00,511
It looks like you got lucky and survived.

791
00:53:09,228 --> 00:53:10,062
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

792
00:53:12,565 --> 00:53:13,900
No!

793
00:53:28,956 --> 00:53:30,416
That hurt, right?

794
00:53:30,499 --> 00:53:31,834
-Are you okay?
-Damn it.

795
00:53:31,918 --> 00:53:33,920
Can you stand up on your own?

796
00:53:40,551 --> 00:53:41,636
You're out.

797
00:53:43,262 --> 00:53:46,098
No secretary should attack
their superior under any circumstances.

798
00:53:46,641 --> 00:53:47,600
Disqualified.

799
00:53:49,644 --> 00:53:51,687
Go with Candidate Nine. I'm going home.

800
00:53:54,065 --> 00:53:55,608
Damn it.

801
00:53:55,691 --> 00:53:56,567
Oh, dear.

802
00:53:57,944 --> 00:53:58,903
All right.

803
00:54:01,572 --> 00:54:04,116
I was told to be careful.

804
00:54:05,826 --> 00:54:07,244
Kang Jae-hee.

805
00:54:07,328 --> 00:54:09,956
You were almost there.
Why did you have to do that?

806
00:54:20,091 --> 00:54:21,300
Yoon Yi-jun.

807
00:54:22,802 --> 00:54:24,261
It's Yoon Yi-jun!

808
00:54:24,845 --> 00:54:26,055
Bring back my daughter!

809
00:54:26,138 --> 00:54:28,516
-Bring back my daughter!
-Bring her back!

810
00:54:28,599 --> 00:54:29,976
-Back off!
-Bring her back!

811
00:54:30,059 --> 00:54:31,811
-Bring back my sister!
-Bring her back!

812
00:54:31,894 --> 00:54:34,105
Yoon Yi-jun! You murdering bastard!

813
00:54:39,986 --> 00:54:42,196
Let me go!

814
00:54:42,279 --> 00:54:44,949
You were the only one there,
you murdering bastard!

815
00:54:45,574 --> 00:54:47,076
My sister!

816
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:50,663
-Let go of me!
-That's not Kang, is it?

817
00:54:50,746 --> 00:54:52,957
-You bastard!
-Damn it.

818
00:54:53,040 --> 00:54:55,084
Bring her back, you scumbag!

819
00:54:56,836 --> 00:54:58,421
You killed her.

820
00:54:58,504 --> 00:54:59,338
Are you okay?

821
00:55:01,799 --> 00:55:02,675
You.

822
00:55:03,634 --> 00:55:05,011
You're that special forces guy.

823
00:55:05,594 --> 00:55:06,721
Yes, I am.

824
00:55:06,804 --> 00:55:08,264
Why did you jump in?

825
00:55:08,347 --> 00:55:10,558
Do you know them?

826
00:55:10,641 --> 00:55:11,684
No.

827
00:55:11,767 --> 00:55:14,311
My priority was to protect you, sir.

828
00:55:15,688 --> 00:55:17,565
So you learn quickly.

829
00:55:18,399 --> 00:55:19,608
What do I do?

830
00:55:19,692 --> 00:55:21,235
You're the first.

831
00:55:22,236 --> 00:55:24,822
The first one who threw himself to save me

832
00:55:30,411 --> 00:55:32,663
and the first one to throw me down.

833
00:55:32,747 --> 00:55:34,623
Please change your mind.

834
00:55:34,707 --> 00:55:36,667
That's why I saved you.

835
00:55:36,751 --> 00:55:38,377
What do I do with you?

836
00:55:42,214 --> 00:55:44,175
If you were a girl,
I'd at least fall for you.

837
00:55:46,135 --> 00:55:48,429
I'm a guy.

838
00:55:50,890 --> 00:55:52,183
Whatever your gender is,

839
00:55:52,266 --> 00:55:55,436
my secretary must put me
as the top priority.

840
00:55:55,519 --> 00:55:56,771
Even if I hate you,

841
00:55:56,854 --> 00:55:59,190
you must like me no matter what.

842
00:55:59,273 --> 00:56:00,357
Under any circumstances.

843
00:56:00,441 --> 00:56:01,650
Are you up to it?

844
00:56:01,734 --> 00:56:02,902
Yes.

845
00:56:02,985 --> 00:56:05,154
You'll be my top priority
under any circumstances.

846
00:56:05,237 --> 00:56:08,908
-And?
-And I will not dislike you

847
00:56:11,494 --> 00:56:14,246
and stay loyal…

848
00:56:16,957 --> 00:56:18,042
And I will like you.

849
00:56:18,793 --> 00:56:19,919
This isn't it.

850
00:56:21,962 --> 00:56:23,130
I will like you!

851
00:56:34,100 --> 00:56:37,019
Start work next Monday.
Come to my house at 9 a.m.

852
00:56:44,485 --> 00:56:46,946
I had to sell my soul there.

853
00:56:47,780 --> 00:56:49,824
I'm going to get you, Yoon Yi-jun.

854
00:56:56,038 --> 00:56:58,791
Kang Jae-hee. I never doubted you.

855
00:56:58,874 --> 00:57:01,335
The captain never trusted you!

856
00:57:07,341 --> 00:57:08,676
You'd better be ready.

857
00:57:08,759 --> 00:57:10,386
It's Korea's number one conglomerate.

858
00:57:10,469 --> 00:57:12,680
We're doing an undercover investigation
at Taekang.

859
00:57:12,763 --> 00:57:15,516
Evidence obtained illegally has no power,

860
00:57:15,599 --> 00:57:16,934
but let's try our best.

861
00:57:17,643 --> 00:57:18,894
This is the beginning.

862
00:57:18,978 --> 00:57:21,147
Let's catch the culprit
and avenge the victim.

863
00:57:21,730 --> 00:57:23,732
I'll find the missing phone.

864
00:57:23,816 --> 00:57:24,942
Trust me!

865
00:57:25,025 --> 00:57:26,527
-Let's do it!
-Before we drink…

866
00:57:27,695 --> 00:57:29,363
from this moment on,

867
00:57:29,446 --> 00:57:30,990
you are banned from drinking.

868
00:57:31,991 --> 00:57:34,160
-I'll stop starting tomorrow.
-Starting today.

869
00:57:34,743 --> 00:57:36,537
The moment your drinking habits come out,

870
00:57:36,620 --> 00:57:38,664
this operation is done for good.
Remember that.

871
00:57:39,373 --> 00:57:40,583
All right.

872
00:57:41,083 --> 00:57:43,752
Gosh, this place had the best pork belly.

873
00:57:43,836 --> 00:57:45,296
-I'm so full.
-Good job.

874
00:57:47,506 --> 00:57:49,466
We couldn't have started anything
without you.

875
00:57:50,426 --> 00:57:51,385
It's nothing.

876
00:57:53,971 --> 00:57:55,598
It won't be easy getting Yoon Yi-jun.

877
00:57:56,599 --> 00:58:00,102
The captain also said
he is something else.

878
00:58:03,480 --> 00:58:05,900
He corners people
without ever revealing his intentions.

879
00:58:06,442 --> 00:58:09,069
I'll find out
whether he did hide the phone.

880
00:58:09,653 --> 00:58:11,113
Let me know if something happens.

881
00:58:11,488 --> 00:58:12,615
I'll go and help.

882
00:58:14,450 --> 00:58:16,035
Are you worried about me?

883
00:58:16,702 --> 00:58:17,536
Are you?

884
00:58:18,204 --> 00:58:19,371
You're worried, right?

885
00:58:22,374 --> 00:58:26,295
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT KANG JAE-HEE

886
00:58:26,378 --> 00:58:27,463
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

887
00:58:29,340 --> 00:58:30,883
KANG JAE-HEE

888
00:58:33,594 --> 00:58:35,095
The tear is bigger than I thought.

889
00:58:35,971 --> 00:58:37,806
I guess I have no choice.

890
00:58:45,397 --> 00:58:48,984
KUNMANDU

891
00:58:49,068 --> 00:58:51,028
Why can't you feed me like this every day?

892
00:58:51,111 --> 00:58:52,655
I can't do this often.

893
00:58:52,738 --> 00:58:54,490
Gosh, something smells really good.

894
00:58:56,283 --> 00:58:58,077
-Come have a seat.
-Come on.

895
00:58:59,078 --> 00:59:00,246
Take a seat.

896
00:59:01,330 --> 00:59:02,331
Here.

897
00:59:04,041 --> 00:59:05,334
You're the best, Mom.

898
00:59:06,919 --> 00:59:09,296
-What about the new one?
-I sent it to the dry cleaner.

899
00:59:09,380 --> 00:59:11,340
I need to wear one tomorrow.

900
00:59:11,423 --> 00:59:13,467
Why can't you come home again for a while?

901
00:59:14,051 --> 00:59:16,553
It's related to the investigation,

902
00:59:16,637 --> 00:59:17,805
so it's a secret.

903
00:59:19,265 --> 00:59:20,808
It's not anything dangerous, right?

904
00:59:20,891 --> 00:59:23,143
Come on, honey.

905
00:59:23,227 --> 00:59:26,063
Do you know how much we've had to pay
in damages for other people?

906
00:59:26,146 --> 00:59:28,440
If you're going to worry,
worry about the other side.

907
00:59:28,899 --> 00:59:29,900
Goodness.

908
00:59:31,443 --> 00:59:33,279
If it weren't for Jae-hee,

909
00:59:33,362 --> 00:59:35,239
you would be out on the streets

910
00:59:35,322 --> 00:59:37,616
after you failed your chicken farm.

911
00:59:37,700 --> 00:59:40,452
If you have any decency,
leave the ribs for her.

912
00:59:42,121 --> 00:59:45,249
If you have any decency,
leave the pork for her as well.

913
00:59:45,833 --> 00:59:47,209
Jeez.

914
00:59:47,293 --> 00:59:49,003
Can I have some of this, Princess?

915
00:59:49,086 --> 00:59:51,797
Of course, Dad. Let me give you some.

916
00:59:51,880 --> 00:59:53,132
Open up.

917
00:59:55,843 --> 00:59:58,721
-You should be grateful to me.
-Why?

918
00:59:58,804 --> 01:00:01,056
Back in the day,
I was the hottest guy in town.

919
01:00:01,140 --> 01:00:03,350
And see? You have my looks.

920
01:00:03,434 --> 01:00:04,560
Be grateful to me.

921
01:00:05,769 --> 01:00:06,812
She takes after me.

922
01:00:08,355 --> 01:00:09,189
After you?

923
01:00:10,691 --> 01:00:12,443
Dad, hurry up and agree with her.

924
01:00:12,526 --> 01:00:14,028
Or else you're dead meat.

925
01:00:29,001 --> 01:00:30,127
Do you also think

926
01:00:31,503 --> 01:00:34,423
I killed Secretary Han?

927
01:01:07,831 --> 01:01:09,708
I'm here. Can you see?

928
01:01:09,792 --> 01:01:11,335
Yes, I can see well.

929
01:01:20,177 --> 01:01:21,220
I'm heading in.

930
01:01:21,303 --> 01:01:22,971
Okay. Be careful.

931
01:02:16,233 --> 01:02:19,528
Hello, sir. I'll be working
as your secretary from today!

932
01:02:25,576 --> 01:02:27,995
This could be a problem, Special Forces.

933
01:02:30,539 --> 01:02:34,001
I was afraid this might be the case.

934
01:02:34,585 --> 01:02:35,419
Don't tell me…

935
01:02:45,888 --> 01:02:46,889
You.

936
01:03:01,570 --> 01:03:03,197
Busted.

937
01:03:04,031 --> 01:03:05,324
Did I get caught?

938
01:03:38,398 --> 01:03:40,150
SPECIAL THANKS TO
JUNG YOO-MIN AND PARK JUN-MUYN

939
01:03:40,234 --> 01:03:42,194
-I will continue to keep my eyes on you.
-What the hell?

940
01:03:42,277 --> 01:03:44,321
And you'll need to keep proving yourself.

941
01:03:45,030 --> 01:03:46,907
He's crazier than I expected.

942
01:03:46,990 --> 01:03:48,367
You'll beat him up soon.

943
01:03:48,450 --> 01:03:50,410
I heard the VIPs are coming
to the chairman's office.

944
01:03:50,494 --> 01:03:51,411
Everyone, get out.

945
01:03:51,495 --> 01:03:53,455
I'm Lee Hye-jung,
Executive Secretary to the Chairman.

946
01:03:53,539 --> 01:03:55,374
The Taekang Goddess may be pretty,

947
01:03:55,457 --> 01:03:57,334
but I don't like her personality.

948
01:03:57,417 --> 01:03:59,002
She saw something before she died?

949
01:03:59,086 --> 01:04:00,879
Did you destroy
everything Secretary Han saw?

950
01:04:00,963 --> 01:04:02,214
The missing phone. That's the key.

951
01:04:02,297 --> 01:04:04,174
Second floor, last room.
You can't go in there.

952
01:04:04,258 --> 01:04:06,301
-It's that room.
-Who are you?

953
01:04:06,385 --> 01:04:07,719
Who sent you?

954
01:04:10,764 --> 01:04:13,767
Translated by Leo Chung
